---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../consts";
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Parenza"
  description="Parenza's formal privacy policy is being finalized alongside our Data Protection Impact Assessment. The Trust & Security page describes our current data handling in full."
  path="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  subhead="In progress — and we'd rather say that than publish boilerplate we haven't stood behind."
>
  <section>
    <p>
      The formal privacy policy is being drafted alongside our Data Protection
      Impact Assessment, and will be published before Parenza opens beyond the
      design-partner cohort. Putting a generic template here in the meantime
      would tell you less than the truth does.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      What we actually collect, where it lives, what happens when you connect
      your own AI assistant, and how to have your data deleted are all described
      in plain language on the{" "}
      <a href="/trust" class="text-pz-clay-strong underline underline-offset-2"
        >Trust &amp; Security</a
      >{" "}page. That page reflects current practice, not aspiration.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      Design partners receive the data-handling terms that apply to them directly
      before onboarding. Questions in the meantime:{" "}
      <a
        href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}
        class="text-pz-clay-strong underline underline-offset-2">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
